# Code owners for this repository.
#
# GitHub applies the LAST matching pattern to a path, and a line that names no
# owner releases the path. There is deliberately no catch-all `*` line: a path
# is owned only because a line below names it. Documents (every `.md` file),
# editor and ignore files, the Node version pin and the lockfile have no line,
# so a change to them needs no code-owner review.
#
# `scripts/codeowners_owned.py` answers "is this path owned" for a fixed table
# of sample paths, one per kept class and one per released class, and its test
# runs in the secret-free job. Edit this file and that table together.

# Pulumi project and stack config. The encrypted config and the image pin sit
# in the same file, so a pin change cannot be released without it.
Pulumi.yaml                @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
Pulumi.*.yaml              @branchLeft/branchleft-admin

# The Pulumi program and what it is built with. `pulumi preview` runs these
# with the stack passphrase in the environment, and this is the code that would
# create a billed resource.
*.ts                       @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
*.tsx                      @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
*.mts                      @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
*.cts                      @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
tsconfig.json              @branchLeft/branchleft-admin

# Install-time inputs. The plan and deploy jobs run `pnpm install` with the
# passphrase, the state keys and the deploy key in reach, `main` here picks the
# program Pulumi runs, and `dependencies` pins the component that creates the
# billed resources. Only the lockfile is released. A dependency bump that
# touches package.json therefore still comes to the owner until the merge route
# can tell a version-only change apart.
package.json               @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
.npmrc                     @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
pnpm-workspace.yaml        @branchLeft/branchleft-admin

# What the deploy's ssh trusts, and what runs on a contributor's machine.
known_hosts                @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
.pre-commit-config.yaml    @branchLeft/branchleft-admin

# Executable code, at any depth, so a new script never arrives unowned. The
# checks and gate tests are here: jobs that hold secrets run the scripts, and
# their output decides whether a deploy is approved.
*.py                       @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
*.sh                       @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
*.js                       @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
*.mjs                      @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
*.cjs                      @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/scripts/testdata/         @branchLeft/branchleft-admin

# The rules and the owner's words.
CLAUDE.md                  @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
AUTHORISATIONS.md          @branchLeft/branchleft-admin

# Legal text.
LICENSE                    @branchLeft/branchleft-admin

# The shared set below is the standards escape hatches, copied byte for byte,
# and must stay the final lines: nothing after or between them. The workflows,
# dependabot.yml and this file are under /.github/.
/.standardsignore        @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/.standards.mode         @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/.docs-lint*             @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/.standards-db-tooling   @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
/.github/                @branchLeft/branchleft-admin
